# Database Conventions

## Schema

- Drizzle ORM schemas live in `server/src/db/schema/`, one file per entity.
- Table/column names use `snake_case` in the database, `camelCase` in TypeScript.
- Use Drizzle's type-safe query builder — no raw SQL unless absolutely necessary.
- All tables include `created_at` and `updated_at` timestamps.
- Use `pgvector` for embedding columns.

## Migrations

- Timestamped migration files in `server/src/db/migrations/`.
- Generate migrations with `drizzle-kit generate`.
- Never hand-edit generated migration SQL unless fixing a conflict.
- Every migration must be reversible in development.

## Seed Data

- Seed scripts live in `server/src/db/seeds/`.
- Seeds are idempotent — safe to run multiple times.

## Example Schema

```typescript
import { pgTable, text, timestamp, uuid } from 'drizzle-orm/pg-core';

export const specs = pgTable('specs', {
  id: uuid('id').primaryKey().defaultRandom(),
  title: text('title').notNull(),
  status: text('status').notNull().default('draft'),
  createdAt: timestamp('created_at').notNull().defaultNow(),
  updatedAt: timestamp('updated_at').notNull().defaultNow(),
});
```

## Anti-patterns

- Raw SQL queries bypassing Drizzle's query builder.
- Missing `notNull()` on required columns.
- Using `camelCase` for database column names.
